        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The relevant portions are extracted hereunder:\n"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b312a3cc29734a44835e15b4c5da1f98_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. Section 42(3) mandates that after receipt of the analysed report, Designated Officer has to send his recommendation within https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 14 days."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "72a67af69eb54f8d9c8f266d179385ef_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, the complaint itself indicate that no such procedure was followed and Section 47 (4) makes it mandatory that once an application is filed for second analysis, it is mandatory on the part of the Officers to provide the sample to get"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b827e7c7ae434e159b54df5041cc3dc4_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n2 Admittedly, in this case such second sample has not been given to the complainant when he has the right to have a second sample analysed, which has been denied."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "428b2146eaed4d3ea6a89d572c4b58d4_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is the serious violation and therefore, this Court is of the view that when the provisions which are mandatory in nature to be complied before initiating any penal action, the same should be complied with rigor."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "dddeccf50ca14734baa249464a54dc0c_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n9. Before driving a person to face a criminal prosecution, the statute which mandates certain procedure, such procedures to be complied first which has not been done in this case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "3d5986bb3d7f48a2850a1d5ad10872a4_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bquashed\\b",
            "matched_text": "quashed",
            "start": 80,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "In this regard, this Court also in similar case in Crl.O.P. No. 774 of 2020 has quashed the prosecution for violation of mandatory provisions of law, which was reported in 2020 SCC OnLine Mad 12748 in the case of G. Irudhayanathan v. B.\nhtt"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "26f184269201417ab053d42df03a1940_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "6.In view of the above, it is clear that the non compliance of the mandate under Section 42 (3) of the Act vitiates the entire proceedings and this Court has taken a consistent view in this regard."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7bca5b520ad6472ba50048852ed741a8_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As a result of the non compliance of the mandate, the petitioners have lost their right to have the second sample analysed before the appropriate Authority."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b40c164f016246a2b6250eb9b9deeb0b_32",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Hence, the continuation of the proceedings against the petitioners will result in abuse of process of Court and it requires the interference of this Court in exercise of its jurisdiction under Section 482 Cr.P.C.\n7.In the result"
      },
